    <h1>About</h1>

    <div class="video-embed">[ intro video goes here ]</div>

    <p>I'm Hasan — a founder in Helsinki, by way of Bangladesh.</p>

    <p>My uncle never wrote a business plan. He saw a thing he wanted, pulled in the people he liked, and moved. As a kid I watched that work, and I copied it without knowing I was copying anything — I built things because building felt like the natural thing a person does with a day. Then I became an immigrant and picked up a second voice, the one that asks <em>lokey ki bolbe</em> — what will people say — before I do anything. A lot of what I write here is the work of taking the chair back from that second voice.</p>

    <p>These days I build companies and write about building them. <strong>Makeshift</strong> is the digital agency I founded — Webflow, AI, and automation for B2B teams across the Nordics and UK. <strong>Zipli</strong> is a food-rescue platform where I'm CTO, in pilots with Sodexo and the City of Helsinki. <strong>Flowtusk</strong> is an automation tool for Webflow. Earlier I co-built Krusti Foodkits, and worked at TietoEVRY and Nordea.</p>

    <p>But the projects aren't the point of this site. The writing is. I care most about the people I build with, about shipping instead of polishing, and about the strange double-vision that comes from running two cultures at once. If any of that resonates, start with <a href="/essays/we-used-to-just-move">We Used to Just Move</a> or <a href="/essays/sent-not-saved">Sent, Not Saved</a>.</p>

    <p>Find me on <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/hasan-shahriar-rhiday/">LinkedIn</a> or <a href="https://github.com/rhiday">GitHub</a>, or read the <a href="/">essays</a>.</p>
  </article>
